WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:10.100
A cryptographically secure, on-chain list of 280 million verified supporters is not an "analogy" or a "metaphor" or a "nice

2
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:15.240
idea.". It is the largest political mandate in human history.

3
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.160
Nothing else comes close. Politicians can ignore protests. They can ignore polls.

4
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:28.260
They can ignore reality for surprisingly long periods (see: climate change, 1970-present).

5
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:37.840
They cannot ignore 280 million cryptographically verified humans saying "do this thing or we vote you out.".

6
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.360
Here's how to build that list. What You're Actually Building.

7
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:48.180
The Goal. Build a privacy-preserving, globally verifiable referendum.

8
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:55.340
It shows public support for a one percent treaty and decentralized institutes of health, or D.I.H.s.

9
00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:04.400
Essentially, a website where people say "please stop letting me die of stupid things" in a way that lawyers find convincing.

10
00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:12.160
Requirements: Must be auditable (so politicians can't claim it's fake, though they will absolutely try).

11
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.560
Must be persuasive (so policymakers actually do their jobs for once).

12
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:25.260
Must hit three point five percent global participation (two hundred eighty million plus verified votes).

13
00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:33.400
That last number isn't arbitrary. Once three point five percent of a population actively supports something, it becomes

14
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.480
unstoppable. Every time. Across all cultures. For centuries.

15
00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:48.440
More on that later. The Principles (Or: How Not to Build a Fraudulent Voting System): Verifiability: Cryptographic proofs

16
00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.040
that votes are real (can't fake the math, though politicians will try).

17
00:01:53.040 --> 00:02:00.760
Privacy: Nobody knows who you voted for (including us). Equity: Works for everyone, including people without bank accounts

18
00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:08.240
or government I.D.s (which is most of Earth, by the way). Transparency: Open-source code so anyone can audit it.

19
00:02:09.139 --> 00:02:12.460
Viral Growth: Needs to spread organically. Target: fifty to sixty-four cents per verified participant (includes referral

20
00:02:12.460 --> 00:03:51.560
payment biometric verification platform overhead). The trick is doing all of these simultaneously.

21
00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.540
It's like juggling while riding a bicycle while the bicycle is on fire.

22
00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:14.100
But the alternative is everyone dies of preventable diseases, so the bicycle stays on fire.

23
00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:52.760
System Architecture (Or: Math That Politicians Can't Argue With).

24
00:04:54.240 --> 00:06:00.400
The voting system uses end-to-end verifiable cryptography: receipts that prove you voted, without proving how you voted.

25
00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:11.500
Politicians can claim polls are fake. They cannot claim math is fake.

26
00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:15.440
(Several have tried. The math won every time.). Each voter gets a cryptographic receipt.

27
00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.960
All ballots are published anonymized. Zero-knowledge proofs guarantee the count is legitimate.

28
00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:20.000
Your biometric data never leaves your device. All code is open-source.

29
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.680
It's the most transparent election in history, which is an embarrassingly low bar.

30
00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:21.960
On Stopping People from Cheating (The Hard Part). Your species has a gift for ruining voting systems.

31
00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:22.020
You've been cheating at democracy since you invented it. Three escalating verification layers: Basic checks (stops about

32
