more than one person, which is how avalanches work). Greater than ninety-nine percent fraud detection with less than one

40
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
percent false positives (the bots stay out, the humans stay in).

41
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
Secondary metrics track geographic distribution, brand awareness, and whether politicians have started sweating yet.

42
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
(The sweat metric is informal but surprisingly reliable. They always sweat before they act.) The Bottom Line.

43
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
Two hundred million dollars for the campaign, funded by VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds.

44
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
Target cost: less than seventy-five cents per verified participant.

45
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
That's cheaper than acquiring a customer for literally any consumer product on Earth.

46
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
You spend more marketing soda. 280 million verified humans saying "do this or lose your job" to every politician on Earth.

47
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
That's not a petition. Petitions are what you ignore. That's a pink slip with 280 million signatures.

48
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
On Why three point five percent Is The Magic Number. The 280 million target isn't pulled from thin air.

49
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
It's based on the "three point five percent Rule," a historical pattern that has held across cultures, centuries, and continents

50
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
with the reliability of a physical law: When three point five percent of a population actively participates in sustained,

51
00:06:22.153 --> 00:06:22.153
